== TARGET (0923835 6b969b46830d5de9c2eb8568d7f792662), macOS/BSD stat ==
exit=0
ok - fm-spawn --relaunch: rebuilds regular env files with source and worker values

Result/limitation: the fix is a pure reorder of the stat(1) fallback chain
(`stat -c '%a' ... || stat -f '%Lp' ...` instead of `stat -f ... || stat -c
...`). On GNU/Linux (the CI runner), `stat -f` is "filesystem status" mode, not
BSD's format flag, so the original order silently produced the wrong
(non-600) value instead of falling through, which is exactly the CI failure
quoted in the user intent. macOS's BSD `stat` has no such ambiguity (`-f` is
always the format flag here), so both the pre-fix and post-fix ordering pass
locally and this host cannot discriminate the two commits for this specific
assertion. No Docker, Linux VM, or local GNU coreutils (`gstat`) is available
on this host, and installing coreutils system-wide/globally is out of bounds
for this run, so the Linux-specific regression itself could not be
reproduced live here. The target scenario pass above is still a direct live
run of the real test against the real product on the available platform.
